<title>HUNGARY: Hungary says Czech crown battle not to harm region.</title>
<headline>Hungary says Czech crown battle not to harm region.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Hungary (NBH) said on Wednesday investment in central Europe as a whole is unlikely to suffer from the Czech crown turmoil.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe that financial investors have learnt about the markets recently,&quot; NBH Deputy President Gyorgy Szapary told a news conference. &quot;They see that this is a Czech problem and they can make difference, seeing the Hungarian macroeconomic figures.&quot;</p>
<p>The Czech National Bank on Monday allowed the crown to float after it was pushed to record lows in the past two weeks by a wave of short-sellings.</p>
<p>-- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
